---
// PHP, "Who our PHP is designed for" (2026-11-18, replaces the photo). A vertical path: where people come from,
// the two kinds of PHP care, and the step down to the addiction IOP (all from the section copy).
import Icon from "../../Icon.astro";
---
<figure class="gx on-dark" aria-label="People come to PHP after a crisis, from inpatient hospitalization, rehab, detox or residential treatment, or when weekly therapy isn't enough. PHP treats depression, anxiety, trauma and mood disorders, and the addiction PHP treats alcohol, drug and prescription drug addiction with SUD groups, MAT when it fits and co-occurring care. As you stabilize you move into the addiction IOP in Glastonbury or Westbrook.">
  <ol class="gx-path">
    <li>
      <span class="gx-path-n i-n"><Icon name="arrow" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>
      <div><b>Coming from</b><small>A crisis · inpatient hospitalization, rehab, detox or residential care · weekly therapy that isn’t enough</small></div>
    </li>
    <li class="is-here">
      <span class="gx-path-n i-g"><Icon name="shield" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>
      <div><b>PHP in Glastonbury</b>
        <div class="gx-path-two">
          <p><span>Mental health</span>Depression, anxiety, trauma, mood disorders</p>
          <p><span>Addiction PHP</span>Alcohol, drug &amp; prescription drug use · SUD groups · MAT when it fits</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="gx-path-n i-s"><Icon name="refresh" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>
      <div><b>As you stabilize</b><small>Step into our <a class="inl" href="/programs/addiction-iop/">Addiction IOP</a> in Glastonbury or Westbrook</small></div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption class="gx-foot"><Icon name="check" class="h-4 w-4" />Support tailored to you, including those at risk of relapse</figcaption>
</figure>
